      {
        "id": 228482,
        "name": "Missingno",
        "username": "Missingno",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/missingno/{size}/2049_2.png",
        "created_at": "2019-08-14T20:41:57.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"TundraWolfe\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/t/958977/48.png\" class=\"avatar\"> TundraWolfe:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<div><b>Missingno wrote:</b><br>\n<blockquote>\" Play Calculated Action. Lifeline takes 0 damage because of reduction. Choose to play 2 cards. Calculated Action moves to trash. (Play Count is 2.) \"<br>\nRight, I'mma stop you right there.  Calculated action doesn't move into the trash until you play both the cards it lets you play.\n</blockquote>\n</div>\n<p>That was a debate we had, actually, so I’m glad someone else pointed it out. Just so we’re clear, until all cards that let you play extra cards are resolved, nothing hits the trash? Must be the part of my brain that’s been trained for Magic: the Gathering that confused things for us.</p>\n<p>If that’s the case, then this obviously doesn’t work as written. How would this interact if Lifeline were given a static ability to “play an additional card during his Play phase”, akin to something like Tachyon’s Pushing the Limits?</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Basically until the effects of all extra card plays are resolved you don’t put the card that gives extra plays into the trash.  For example, if Tach has pushing the limits out and plays Fleet of Foot first, Fleet of Foot will not go into the trash until the card fleet of foot plays is done going off.  Once that card is done Fleet of Foot will go into the trash and then you can play a card provided by Pushing the Limits.  If I’ve worded this poorly I suggest watching the video game adaptation be played as it makes things clearer.</p>\n<p>As a note this also applies to Stuntman’s ongoings.  They don’t enter the trash until all the effects go off which prevents you from chaining Dramatic Cliffhanger with itself.</p>",
        "post_number": 8,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T06:02:58.932Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
        "quote_count": 0,
        "incoming_link_count": 0,
        "reads": 4,
        "readers_count": 3,
        "score": 0.8,
        "yours": false,
        "topic_id": 19368,
        "topic_slug": "lifeline-infinite-damage-combo",
        "display_username": "Missingno",
        "primary_group_name": null,
        "flair_name": null,
        "flair_url": null,
        "flair_bg_color": null,
        "flair_color": null,
        "flair_group_id": null,
        "badges_granted": [],
        "version": 1,
        "can_edit": false,
        "can_delete": false,
        "can_recover": false,
        "can_see_hidden_post": false,
        "can_wiki": false,
        "read": false,
        "user_title": null,
        "bookmarked": false,
        "raw": "[quote=\"TundraWolfe\"]\n\n<div class=\"bb-quote\"><b>Missingno wrote:</b><br />\n<blockquote class=\"bb-quote-body\">\" Play Calculated Action. Lifeline takes 0 damage because of reduction. Choose to play 2 cards. Calculated Action moves to trash. (Play Count is 2.) \"<br />\nRight, I'mma stop you right there.  Calculated action doesn't move into the trash until you play both the cards it lets you play.\n</blockquote>\n</div>\n\nThat was a debate we had, actually, so I'm glad someone else pointed it out. Just so we're clear, until all cards that let you play extra cards are resolved, nothing hits the trash? Must be the part of my brain that's been trained for Magic: the Gathering that confused things for us.\n\nIf that's the case, then this obviously doesn't work as written. How would this interact if Lifeline were given a static ability to \"play an additional card during his Play phase\", akin to something like Tachyon's Pushing the Limits?\n\n[/quote]\n\nBasically until the effects of all extra card plays are resolved you don't put the card that gives extra plays into the trash.  For example, if Tach has pushing the limits out and plays Fleet of Foot first, Fleet of Foot will not go into the trash until the card fleet of foot plays is done going off.  Once that card is done Fleet of Foot will go into the trash and then you can play a card provided by Pushing the Limits.  If I've worded this poorly I suggest watching the video game adaptation be played as it makes things clearer.\n\nAs a note this also applies to Stuntman's ongoings.  They don't enter the trash until all the effects go off which prevents you from chaining Dramatic Cliffhanger with itself.",
